// Originally generated by `scripts/gen/wasm_simd.py`; now maintained by hand (the generator is out of date).
//! # Auto slice ops (wasm32)
//!
//! Whole-buffer elementwise work without picking a token by hand. Each fn
//! reads [`super::detect_features`] (`cfg` plus the runtime flags, see
//! [`super::enable_simd128`]) and takes the best rung:
//!
//! 1. `RelaxedSimd` - FMA family only, and only with the
//!    `wasm-relaxed-simd` cargo feature or `+relaxed-simd`.
//! 2. [`Simd128`] - everything here.
//! 3. scalar (`auto_down`, private), same lane semantics.
//!
//! Also reachable as [`super::auto`] (alias), same naming as
//! `x86::auto_up` and `aarch64::auto_up`.
//!
//! ```
//! # #[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")] {
//! use miraculix::wasm::auto_up;
//! let a = [1i32, 2, 3, 4, 5];
//! let b = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50];
//! let mut out = [0i32; 5];
//! auto_up::add_i32(&a, &b, &mut out);
//! assert_eq!(out, [11, 22, 33, 44, 55]);
//! # }
//! ```
//!
//! ## Shared contract
//!
//! - Lengths of inputs and `out` must match. Mismatch **panics** (on every
//!   rung, checked before dispatch).
//! - Integer `add`/`sub`/`mul` wrap. `qadd`/`qsub` saturate. `avg` is the
//!   rounding average.
//! - **Mask.** Compares write all-1s or 0, **unsigned**, as wide as the
//!   input (`cmpeq_i8 -> u8`, `cmpeq_f64 -> u64`), as on aarch64.
//! - **Select.** `select_*(a, b, mask, out)` takes `b` where the mask bit is
//!   set and `a` where it is clear, **per bit** (`v128.bitselect`).
//! - **Andnot.** `andnot_*(a, b)` is `a & !b` (Arm `BIC`). x86 `pandn` is
//!   `!a & b`.
//! - **Shifts.** x86 shape: `shl_i32::<IMM>(a, out)` with one constant
//!   count. `shr` is logical (zeros in, also for signed lanes), `sra`
//!   arithmetic. `IMM` at or above the lane width is a compile error (wasm
//!   would take it modulo the width, x86 would give 0). wasm has no per-lane
//!   shift count, so aarch64's `SSHL` form is not offered.
//! - **FMA.** On [`Simd128`] and scalar: `a * b` rounded, then added (two
//!   roundings), bit-identical between those two rungs. On `RelaxedSimd`
//!   the engine picks fused or unfused per lane.
//! - **Float min/max.** wasm semantics on every rung: NaN if either input is
//!   NaN, `-0.0 < +0.0`. Not Rust's `f32::min` (which prefers the number).
//! - **NaN bits.** wasm leaves the payload of a NaN result open, so NaN
//!   results agree as NaN, not bit for bit.
//! - `sum_f32`/`sum_f64` are grouped by vector lane, so not bit-identical
//!   to a left-to-right fold on inexact data. The scalar rung uses the same
//!   grouping, so all rungs agree.
//!
//! ## Not here
//!
//! Ops wasm has no instruction for stay off this layer instead of being
//! emulated: `mul_i8`/`mul_u8`, 64-bit `min`/`max`, ordered `u64` compares,
//! `hadd`/`hsub`, `popcnt` wider than `u8`. Token-only: `sqrt`/rounding
//! (`core` has no scalar fallback under `no_std`), `swizzle`, dot products,
//! `q15mulr`, and the relaxed min/max/laneselect/trunc.

